==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|guerilla}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|es|guerrilla}}, diminutive of {{m|es|guerra||war}}, coined during the {{w|Peninsular War}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ɡəˈɹɪlə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-guerrilla.wav|Audio (US)}}
* {{homophones|en|gorilla}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[soldier]] in a small independent group, fighting against the government or regular forces by [[surprise]] [[raid]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The right-wing paramilitary's offensive against the Marxist '''guerrillas''' failed because they did not know the terrain well enough.}}
# {{lb|en|now|_|rare}} A non-official war carried out by small independent groups; a [[guerrilla war]].

